Z||000000||topcat||12-25-2001||05:50 PM||||I own a 86 SE with the V-6.  I want to swap the AM/FM/Cassette for a Delco model with the CD palyer.  Anyone know of a model from some other GM vehicle that will fit the opening perfectly.  I want to retain somewhat of an factory original look, so the aftermarket models are out (I took the Alpine that the previous owner installed out, and put the original back in).  I am good at reading wire diagrams, so doing a little wire work is no problem.  I just need a perfect fit for the one that I chose.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierokid87||12-25-2001||06:23 PM||||Any radio from a Pontiac Firebird will fit.  I know that much.  if you want a newer one go with like a 94-97.  Those I think look closest to the Fiero one.  I just threw the years that I knwo Firebird had those CD players.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierokid87||12-25-2001||06:28 PM||||sorry I should have just said 94 and up.<P>Scott||||reg||1
