Z||000004||Oreif||12-25-2001||06:49 PM||||This place sells Delco Radio's (all kinds and years) and the harness adapters to hook them up in your Fiero.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mnrelectronics.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mnrelectronics.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">            <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||topcat||12-25-2001||07:31 PM||||Thanks for the website... I have used them in the past for my Catera Delco Bose CD Changer.  They are pretty good<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT GT 87||12-25-2001||07:44 PM||||The size of the Fiero opening is called Din and a half , or 1&1/2 a standard size unit . Pioneer has a dinand a half CD player . I put one in my wifes '94 Camaro , it is a real nice unit . About 220$ i think . There are several other aftermarket ones out there , or pick from any of the newer Firebird or Camaro s .||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroMGDriver||12-25-2001||10:02 PM||||I got a universal mount CD player from M and R Electronics.  I believe it came from a 94 model year.  Perfect fit, looks great, and they also sold me a wiring harness to make the intallation a snap.  This is the way to go.||||reg||1
